[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739822294","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104366#issuecomment-2739822294","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104366","id":2739822294,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jTl7W","user":{"login":"runbozhuang","id":13036245,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDM2MjQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13036245?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang","html_url":"https://github.com/runbozhuang","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/runbozhuang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-20T10:06:26Z","updated_at":"2025-03-20T10:06:26Z","body":"Working on it, will push and reopen this later","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2739822294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745278021","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104366#issuecomment-2745278021","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104366","id":2745278021,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6joZ5F","user":{"login":"EricEzaM","id":41730826,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNzMwODI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41730826?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM","html_url":"https://github.com/EricEzaM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EricEzaM/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-22T13:55:25Z","updated_at":"2025-03-22T14:00:37Z","body":"I don't think this is the correct fix. What you have identified and fixed is the _symptom_ (i.e. the `Tree` control seems to be \"stealing\" shortcuts from other controls), rather than using the symptom to find the root cause of the issue (a bug in the way global editor shortcuts are handled).\r\n\r\n> Shortcut should not be accepted in void EditorProperty::shortcut_input(const Ref &p_event) when focus_owner is Tree\r\n\r\nThis is kind of right. But `Tree` is not the problem, but rather the shortcut being triggered in a context where it has no business being triggered (the editor property is not even displayed!). Setting the context has a way of being done already using the shortcut system that is generic and does not need case-specific code like this. It is `set_shortcut_context(const Node* p_node)`. Setting the shortcut context on say, an `EditorProperty` to the root `EditorInspector` will ensure that the shortcuts on the property are only triggered if the inspector is the current \"context\". With the current implementation, a node is an active \"context\" if the viewport focus is on any descendant of that node.\r\n\r\nLinked below is my PR that uses this. I think the only change really necessary is the one in `editor_inspector.cpp` but while I was looking at the code I figured that the \"default case\" logic in `scene_tree.cpp` could also be improved so that it is somewhat more predictable. It's still not ideal though.\r\n\r\nI think part of the problem with the \"shortcut context\" system is that by default, every single node will have its `shortcut_input` be **global** unless it opts-in to the context system by using `set_shortcut_context`. This means if someone forgets to use `set_shortcut_context` when writing some UI, the shortcuts can be pretty messed up since everything is considered global.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't seem like it is leading developers to the \"pit of success\". I'm not sure if there is a good way to fix it, but perhaps the logic should somehow be flipped so that being a **global** shortcut  is **opt-in**. In this scenario, by default all controls would essentially have `set_shortcut_context(this)` in their constructor. That could be overridden on a case-by-case basis to give shortcuts a larger scope.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745278021/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2745291093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104366#issuecomment-2745291093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104366","id":2745291093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6jodFV","user":{"login":"runbozhuang","id":13036245,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMDM2MjQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13036245?v=4","gravatar_id":"","u